From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Afonchenko <undermove1@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 14:27:23 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] Meridian: AI subscriptions by the person's names, with a
 picker per space and New spaces
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Settings › AI showed accounts as chips ("Default · no space yet") whose
click only opened a small editor, and "Default" named two different
folders. Each AI tool with accounts now has one block:

- Each subscription by the person's own name (click it to rename in
  place); imported folders read "Claude (~/.claude)", "Claude Work",
  never a bare "Default". One true status: Signed in / Needs sign-in
  [Sign in] / Update needed [Update] / Not installed, and its browser
  tools (connected / Connect). Remove is in a ⋯ menu: "Remove from
  Meridian — the folder stays".
- "+ Add Claude" asks only for a name: Meridian makes a private folder
  under its own AI Accounts folder (beside its profiles), starts the
  newest CLI's own sign-in for it (CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR / CODEX_HOME), and
  the row turns ✓ when that is done. Copilot keeps its accounts itself
  and isn't offered Add.
- "Claude in each space": one picker per space and "New spaces", the
  main subscription that new spaces and spaces that never chose follow
  (ai_main_account; absent = the CLI's default, as before). The space
  menu shows and sets the same choice. One account: just "Claude ✓
  Signed in", no picker.
- 1.4/1.5 prefs keep working: same ids, same space choices; a kept
  "Default" label reads as the folder's name.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SwxrQ2eLfJ2bv8cCoG2va1
